  "notes": "{抱|いだ}く is a literary/formal verb with two main uses: physically holding someone in one's arms, and figuratively harboring feelings or ideas. The figurative sense is far more common in modern usage.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {抱|いだ}いている: is harboring/holding (ongoing state)\n\nCOMMON OBJECTS (figurative):\n- ⟦{夢|ゆめ}→夢：01519_yume⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to have a dream/aspiration\n- ⟦{疑問|ぎもん}→疑問：02648_gimon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to harbor doubts\n- ⟦{希望|きぼう}→希望：00221_kibou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to have hope\n- ⟦{不安|ふあん}→不安：00836_fuan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to feel anxiety\n- ⟦{野心|やしん}→野心：15757_yashin⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to harbor ambition\n- ⟦{恨|うら}み→恨み：00414_urami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{抱|いだ}く: to bear a grudge\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{抱|だ}く→抱く：02131_daku⟧: same kanji, more common for physical holding; also colloquial\n- ⟦{抱|かか}える→抱える：02031_kakaeru⟧: to carry/hold in arms; also figurative for \"having\" problems",
